            "learn": {
                "paragraphs": [
                    "**1. Terminating:** The decimal expansion ends (e.g., $7/8 = 0.875$).",
                    "**2. Non-terminating Repeating:** A block of digits repeats (e.g., $1/3 = 0.3\\overline{3}$).",
                    "**3. Irrational Numbers:** Decimals that are **non-terminating and non-repeating** (e.g., $\\sqrt{2}, \\pi$).",
                    "**4. Characterization:** A number is rational if and only if its decimal expansion is either terminating or non-terminating repeating."
